				"He has appeared in more films than any other Disney character. Donald Duck has appeared in over 150 animated short films in the golden age of American animation, several of which were recognized at the [[Academy Awards]]. Donald's first appearance was in the Silly Symphony film The Wise Little Hen (1934), but was reworked as a temperamental comic foil to Mickey Mouse in Orphan's Benefit. In the 1930s, he typically appeared as part of a comic trio with Mickey and Goofy and was given his own film series starting with Don Donald (1937). These films introduced Donald's love interest and permanent girlfriend Daisy Duck and often included his three nephews Huey, Dewey, and Louie. Donald gradually outshone Mickey, who was relegated to a side character in newer cartoons while Donald maintained his own series until 1961",
